00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:37.520
First result, a big chunk of the Jews, they separated themselves from the rest of Judaism. And this they would call the Karaites. They thought that there was so much nonsense predicated and preached in the name of Tora that they completely cut themselves out of the rest of Judaism. And they were called the Karaites.

00:11:38.520 --> 00:12:01.520
And you know that because the government recognized only as one official religion, one official Jewish religion, the Karaites, they came to the government and they said, we are a different religion. And they said, how? They said, well, we don't believe in the Talmud. We don't believe in the Talmud. We only believe in the written law.

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:17.520
The truth is that they believed in tradition. But they had to present this position in order to make it official that they are no longer under the jurisdiction of Teresh Galutah or the Rosh ha-Shana. One thing.

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:36.520
But now because there was no longer a central authority, somebody that everybody respected, Jews became fragmented. They stopped living themselves. And then sects, here and there, little sects, every small group becomes a different sect.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:51.520
And they appear, and when they go to the government, they say, well, we are a different religion. And they become different sects. And the Jewish people become fragmented, divided, and they become weak. Do you understand the situation now?

00:12:51.520 --> 00:13:14.520
The Tora. Today if you want to know about Judaism, you go to a bookshop and buy hundreds of books in English. You want to know about Talmud? The Talmud is available in English. There are explanations of the Talmud in, say, Rashi.

